## Interior terminal vertex and Type-II face floor

The cancellation proof extends to the complete contact complex after
mapping all bounded nonquadrilateral facial terminal occurrences to
one auxiliary graph vertex. The component containing that vertex costs
one in the component count, however many actual inner faces it joins.
Every other small component retains paired cancellation exactly.
No physical source point or face is identified or moved.

Additional canonical inputs on Audit.133: Section 63's distinguished
outer occurrences, Section 67's connected core and face geometry,
Audit.129's fixed-limit atomic track mass, and Audit.131's exact
complete-train count including singleton contacts. The new report
reconstructs the graph argument at this all-topology scope.

The new candidate chain is:

    atomic complete-train mass <= (2f-k)/D
      -> 2f-k >= 2*sqrt(pi/(2*sqrt(3)))*D-o(D)
      -> 4(q-k)-k-2z >= (2*pi+2*sqrt(pi/(2*sqrt(3))))*D-o(D)
      -> (q-k)/D >= 2.0469527302-o(1)
      -> the entire Type-II (q-k)/D <= 1.860 branch is empty.

It also gives f/D >= sqrt(pi/(2*sqrt(3)))-o(1). The high-(q-k)/D
Type-II branch and the macroscopic-container branch remain open.
The source retains every contact isolate through the imported canonical
premises. Neither graph counting nor the face floor supplies a motion,
a uniform face-width bound, or a full Level I contradiction.

